      <p>Modern alkaline cells contain no mercury (unlike some legacy formulations). Zinc, manganese, potassium hydroxide are all relatively low-hazard at end of life. Cells can leak potassium hydroxide if severely discharged and left installed — the white crystalline residue seen in old remote controls.</p>
